":"EU CosIng","Last_Updated":"2026-05-12"},{"INCI_Name":"Sodium Lauroyl Glutamate","CAS_Number":"29923-31-7","EC_Number":"N/A","Chemical_Name":"Sodium N-lauroyl glutamate","Function":"Surfactant (mild anionic / amino acid-derived)","Category_Code":"SURF","Category_Name":"Surfactant","Ingredient_Origin":"Semi-synthetic (glutamic acid + lauric acid)","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"0.50","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"None","Allergen_Flag":"None","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"No specific limit","Max_Concentration_India":"No formal limit","Format_Restriction":"Both","Baby_Restriction":"None","Common_Products":"Premium cleansers Japanese-influenced formulas gentle foams","Key_Safety_Notes":"Amino acid-derived anionic surfactant; very mild; skin-identical amino acid base; good lather feel; COSMOS-approved; popular in Japan; excellent tolerability","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng; COSMOS","Last_Updated":"2026-05-12"},{"INCI_Name":"Retinyl Palmitate","CAS_Number":"79-81-2","EC_Number":"201-228-5","Chemical_Name":"Retinol hexadecanoate / Vitamin A palmitate","Function":"Active (retinoid)","Category_Code":"ACT","Category_Name":"Active Ingredient","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic / Animal-derived","Concern_Level_TCS":"Medium","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"Annex III","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"No","Natural_ISO16128":"0.00","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"None","Allergen_Flag":"Yes","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"0.3% as retinol equivalent (total retinoid EU limit including all forms)","Max_Concentration_India":"No formal limit","Format_Restriction":"Leave-on","Baby_Restriction":"Avoid in pregnancy; not for infants","Common_Products":"Anti-aging serums moisturisers sunscreens (historical)","Key_Safety_Notes":"Ester form of retinol, requires conversion in skin to retinaldehyde then retinoic acid; less potent and slower onset than retinol but better tolerated; EU SCCS opinion (SCCS/1576/16 updated 2022) restricts all retinoids (as retinol equivalents) to 0.3% face/0.05% body leave-on; pregnancy concern (CMR 1B at high doses, precautionary approach for cosmetics); FDA photosensitivity concern for sunscreen use (2020), avoid in SPF products","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"Yes","Source_Reference":"EU Annex III; SCCS/1576/16 + 2022 update; FDA 2020 sunscreen assessment","Last_Updated":"2026-05-12"},{"INCI_Name":"Retinaldehyde","CAS_Number":"116-31-4","EC_Number":"204-132-4","Chemical_Name":"All-trans-retinaldehyde / Retinal / Vitamin A aldehyde","Function":"Active (retinoid)","Category_Code":"ACT","Category_Name":"Active Ingredient","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Medium","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"Annex III","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"0.00","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"None","Allergen_Flag":"Yes","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"0.3% as retinol equivalent (EU Annex III total retinoid limit)","Max_Concentration_India":"No formal limit","Format_Restriction":"Leave-on","Baby_Restriction":"Avoid in pregnancy; not for infants","Common_Products":"High-performance anti-aging serums","Key_Safety_Notes":"Retinal (one step before retinoic acid); more potent than retinol; faster conversion to retinoic acid in skin; subject to EU 0.3% retinol equivalent limit; significant irritation potential especially at first use; typically formulated at <0.1% by brands; pregnancy precautionary avoidance applies; emerging ingredient in prestige anti-aging segment","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"Yes","Source_Reference":"EU Annex III; SCCS/1576/16 + 2022; CIR","Last_Updated":"2026-05-12"},{"INCI_Name":"Hydroxypinacolone Retinoate","CAS_Number":"893412-73-2","EC_Number":"N/A","Chemical_Name":"Granactive Retinoid / Retinoate ester","Function":"Active (retinoid ester)","Category_Code":"ACT","Category_Name":"Active Ingredient","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low-Medium","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"0.00","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"None","Allergen_Flag":"None","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"No EU Annex III entry (not explicitly listed, under review)","Max_Concentration_India":"No formal limit","Format_Restriction":"Leave-on","Baby_Restriction":"Caution in pregnancy, retinoate","Common_Products":"Serums anti-aging products","Key_Safety_Notes":"Retinoic acid ester that binds directly to nuclear retinoic acid receptors without conversion chain; claimed to be non-irritating retinoid; no direct EU restriction yet (regulatory position evolving, check current status); marketed as 'Granactive Retinoid' by Grant Industries; higher cost than retinol; pregnancy: caution (retinoate ester of retinoic acid, precautionary avoidance recommended)","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"Yes","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng; brand technical data; regulatory monitoring required","Last_Updated":"2026-05-12"},{"INCI_Name":"Retinyl Acetate","CAS_Number":"127-47-9","EC_Number":"204-844-2","Chemical_Name":"Retinol acetate / Vitamin A acetate","Function":"Active (retinoid)","Category_Code":"ACT","Category_Name":"Active Ingredient","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Medium","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"Annex III","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"No","Natural_ISO16128":"0.00","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"None","Allergen_Flag":"Yes","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"0.3% as retinol equivalent (EU Annex III total retinoid limit)","Max_Concentration_India":"No formal limit","Format_Restriction":"Leave-on","Baby_Restriction":"Avoid in pregnancy; not for infants